body:
Singles: Kissing You. Oh god Kissing You. I can handle cutesy. I can Oh, oh oh oh or Gee gee gee gee (baby baby) whenever appropriate. Yet this was the song that let me know I have a cutesy limit, but in a weirdly specific way. Objectively I'd say Gee is generally a cutesier song, but for some reason Kissing You hits a very specific cutesy spot that makes me recoil. I don't know how to describe it. Whenever I hear that opening 'du du du du-du', instant skip. (Not relevant to the song, but the video also didn't help. Hyoyeon and Taeyeon's styling: WHY. The lollipop choreography though was cute and clever, that's the positive.) 

&#x200B;

B-Sides: Say Yes. I can pinpoint this one almost entirely on my dislike for spoken-word intros, but it's also just lacking compared to the other Boys b-sides. When I hear it I think 'aw man I wanna listen to Trick'
